{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI now models approvals, generic pauses, and client-tool execution as\nAG-UI interrupt descriptors. Native runs end with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED.outcome.type === 'interrupt'"},{"type":"text","value":", and the continuation is a new run\nwhose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" is the interrupted run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is no codemod. Migrate the server lifecycle and client rendering together.\nLegacy readers stay temporarily for old streams but cannot provide the full\nnative contract. Start from "},{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-mapping","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API mapping"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated / legacy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingInterrupts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingInterrupts"},{"type":"text","value":" is a deprecated alias of the same array)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient.getPendingInterrupts()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient.getInterrupts()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolApprovalResponse({ id, approved })"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Find the bound "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-approval"},{"type":"text","value":" item, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.resolveInterrupt(approved)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeInterrupts(entries, state)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bound item methods or root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupts(...)"},{"type":"text","value":"; reserve "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeInterruptsUnsafe"},{"type":"text","value":" for validated recovery tooling"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"},{"type":"text","value":" custom event"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" interrupt descriptor, reason "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool_call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-input-available"},{"type":"text","value":" custom event"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" interrupt descriptor, reason "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack:client_tool_execution"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Boolean denial treated as cancellation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt(false)"},{"type":"text","value":" for denial; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel()"},{"type":"text","value":" for payloadless cancellation"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolResult"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" removed. It still handles client-tool results and\ndelegates to a matching native item. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval"},{"type":"text","value":" remains the tool-definition\nswitch for approvals."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"single-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Single approval"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Before\nawait addToolApprovalResponse({ id: approval.id, approved: true })\n\n// After\nconst interrupt = interrupts.find(\n  (item) => item.kind === 'tool-approval' && item.toolName === 'transfer',\n)\nif (interrupt?.kind === 'tool-approval' && interrupt.toolName === 'transfer') {\n  interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A valid singleton submits automatically. For the full render/resolve component\nsee "},{"type":"link","href":"./tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool Approval"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"branch-payloads-and-edits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Branch payloads and edits"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Legacy boolean approvals couldn't carry typed data. Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approvalSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" and\nresolve the selected branch with data under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"payload"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true, {\n  editedArgs: { amount: 12, recipient: 'Ada' }, // optional, approval-only, full replacement\n  payload: { note: 'Reviewed' },\n})\ninterrupt.resolveInterrupt(false, { payload: { reason: 'Policy limit' } })","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rejection never accepts edits; top-level custom fields are invalid. A single\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approvalSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" (not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ approve, reject }"},{"type":"text","value":") applies to the selected decision;\nwith no schema the boolean shorthand stays valid."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"denial-vs-cancellation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Denial vs cancellation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt(false, ...)"},{"type":"text","value":" continues the model with an explicit rejected\ndecision. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancel()"},{"type":"text","value":" emits AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status: 'cancelled'"},{"type":"text","value":" and never validates or\nselects the reject branch. Deprecated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolApprovalResponse({ approved: false })"},{"type":"text","value":"\nmaps to denial, not cancellation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"batches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Batches"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native batches are all-or-nothing. Replace approval-ID loops with staged items\n(the last valid item auto-submits) or one synchronous root callback:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resolveInterrupts((interrupt) => {\n  if (interrupt.kind === 'tool-approval') {\n    interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true, { payload: { note: 'Batch review' } })\n    return\n  }\n  interrupt.cancel()\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupts(true|false)"},{"type":"text","value":" is shorthand only for all-approval batches with\nno payload/edits. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelInterrupts()"},{"type":"text","value":" for payloadless all-items cancel,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearResolution()"},{"type":"text","value":" to drop one draft, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retryInterrupts()"},{"type":"text","value":" only when every item\nis still validly staged and the root error is retryable. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./multiple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multiple Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"generic-responses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic responses"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Don't derive a static type from a received "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"responseSchema"},{"type":"text","value":". Parse as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", convert with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z.fromJSONSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", then resolve the validated value.\nFull form example in "},{"type":"link","href":"./generic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server events"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A native server emits, in order: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT"},{"type":"text","value":" → optional\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"STATE_SNAPSHOT"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" with a nonempty interrupt outcome.\nContinuations use a fresh "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runId"},{"type":"text","value":", the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":", and the interrupted run\nas "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":", with every pending ID present exactly once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupts run "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ephemerally"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the server reconstructs and validates the\nexpected batch from the submitted history and its current tool definitions, so\na stateless route needs no persistence. Because the batch is rebuilt from\nclient-provided input, this mode does not provide authoritative recovery,\nexactly-once, replay protection, or restart recovery."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeInterruptsUnsafe"},{"type":"text","value":" is a low-level escape hatch for submitting validated\nraw resume entries directly, not the normal target for approval UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"legacy-limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Legacy limits"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated readers recognize well-formed historical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-input-available"},{"type":"text","value":" events and convert a fully-covered legacy batch into one\ncloned-history follow-up. They do "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" support edited arguments, custom\napproval payloads, generic responses, payloadless cancellation, or expiry/\nschema-hash reconciliation; those fail with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"legacy-unsupported"},{"type":"text","value":". Native and\nlegacy items cannot mix in one batch; a failed legacy transport keeps staged\ndecisions and reports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"legacy-submit-failed"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace native custom-event writers with the interrupt terminal."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render bound "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingInterrupts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace boolean approval helpers with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" + explicit\ndenial/cancellation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace approval loops with atomic batch staging or root "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveInterrupts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolResult"},{"type":"text","value":" for client-tool results where useful."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test expired items and failed transport before removing legacy support."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"api-mapping","text":"API mapping","level":2},{"id":"single-approval","text":"Single approval","level":2},{"id":"branch-payloads-and-edits","text":"Branch payloads and edits","level":2},{"id":"denial-vs-cancellation","text":"Denial vs cancellation","level":2},{"id":"batches","text":"Batches","level":2},{"id":"generic-responses","text":"Generic responses","level":2},{"id":"server-events","text":"Server events","level":2},{"id":"legacy-limits","text":"Legacy limits","level":2},{"id":"checklist","text":"Checklist","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack AI now models approvals, generic pauses, and client-tool execution as\nAG-UI interrupt descriptors. Native runs end with\n`RUN_FINISHED.outcome.type === 'interrupt'`, and the continuation is a new run\nwhose `parentRunId` is the interrupted run.\n\nThere is no codemod. Migrate the server lifecycle and client rendering together.\nLegacy readers stay temporarily for old streams but cannot provide the full\nnative contract. Start from [Overview](./overview).\n\n## API mapping\n\n| Deprecated / legacy | Current |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pendingInterrupts` | `interrupts` (`pendingInterrupts` is a deprecated alias of the same array) |\n| `ChatClient.getPendingInterrupts()` | `ChatClient.getInterrupts()` |\n| `addToolApprovalResponse({ id, approved })` | Find the bound `tool-approval` item, call `interrupt.resolveInterrupt(approved)` |\n| Raw `resumeInterrupts(entries, state)` | Bound item methods or root `resolveInterrupts(...)`; reserve `resumeInterruptsUnsafe` for validated recovery tooling |\n| `approval-requested` custom event | `RUN_FINISHED` interrupt descriptor, reason `tool_call` |\n| `tool-input-available` custom event | `RUN_FINISHED` interrupt descriptor, reason `tanstack:client_tool_execution` |\n| Boolean denial treated as cancellation | `resolveInterrupt(false)` for denial; `cancel()` for payloadless cancellation |\n\n`addToolResult` is **not** removed. It still handles client-tool results and\ndelegates to a matching native item. `needsApproval` remains the tool-definition\nswitch for approvals.\n\n## Single approval\n\n```ts ignore\n// Before\nawait addToolApprovalResponse({ id: approval.id, approved: true })\n\n// After\nconst interrupt = interrupts.find(\n  (item) => item.kind === 'tool-approval' && item.toolName === 'transfer',\n)\nif (interrupt?.kind === 'tool-approval' && interrupt.toolName === 'transfer') {\n  interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)\n}\n```\n\nA valid singleton submits automatically. For the full render/resolve component\nsee [Tool Approval](./tool-approval).\n\n## Branch payloads and edits\n\nLegacy boolean approvals couldn't carry typed data. Add `approvalSchema` and\nresolve the selected branch with data under `payload`:\n\n```ts ignore\ninterrupt.resolveInterrupt(true, {\n  editedArgs: { amount: 12, recipient: 'Ada' }, // optional, approval-only, full replacement\n  payload: { note: 'Reviewed' },\n})\ninterrupt.resolveInterrupt(false, { payload: { reason: 'Policy limit' } })\n```\n\nRejection never accepts edits; top-level custom fields are invalid. A single\n`approvalSchema` (not `{ approve, reject }`) applies to the selected decision;\nwith no schema the boolean shorthand stays valid.\n\n## Denial vs cancellation\n\n`resolveInterrupt(false, ...)` continues the model with an explicit rejected\ndecision. `cancel()` emits AG-UI `status: 'cancelled'` and never validates or\nselects the reject branch. Deprecated `addToolApprovalResponse({ approved: false })`\nmaps to denial, not cancellation.\n\n## Batches\n\nNative batches are all-or-nothing. Replace approval-ID loops with staged items\n(the last valid item auto-submits) or one synchronous root callback:\n\n```ts ignore\nresolveInterrupts((interrupt) => {\n  if (interrupt.kind === 'tool-approval') {\n    interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true, { payload: { note: 'Batch review' } })\n    return\n  }\n  interrupt.cancel()\n})\n```\n\n`resolveInterrupts(true|false)` is shorthand only for all-approval batches with\nno payload/edits. Use `cancelInterrupts()` for payloadless all-items cancel,\n`clearResolution()` to drop one draft, `retryInterrupts()` only when every item\nis still validly staged and the root error is retryable. See\n[Multiple Interrupts](./multiple).\n\n## Generic responses\n\nDon't derive a static type from a received `responseSchema`. Parse as\n`unknown`, convert with `z.fromJSONSchema`, then resolve the validated value.\nFull form example in [Generic Interrupts](./generic).\n\n## Server events\n\nA native server emits, in order: `MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT` → optional\n`STATE_SNAPSHOT` → `RUN_FINISHED` with a nonempty interrupt outcome.\nContinuations use a fresh `runId`, the same `threadId`, and the interrupted run\nas `parentRunId`, with every pending ID present exactly once.\n\nInterrupts run **ephemerally**: the server reconstructs and validates the\nexpected batch from the submitted history and its current tool definitions, so\na stateless route needs no persistence. Because the batch is rebuilt from\nclient-provided input, this mode does not provide authoritative recovery,\nexactly-once, replay protection, or restart recovery.\n\n`resumeInterruptsUnsafe` is a low-level escape hatch for submitting validated\nraw resume entries directly, not the normal target for approval UI.\n\n## Legacy limits\n\nDeprecated readers recognize well-formed historical `approval-requested` and\n`tool-input-available` events and convert a fully-covered legacy batch into one\ncloned-history follow-up. They do **not** support edited arguments, custom\napproval payloads, generic responses, payloadless cancellation, or expiry/\nschema-hash reconciliation; those fail with `legacy-unsupported`. Native and\nlegacy items cannot mix in one batch; a failed legacy transport keeps staged\ndecisions and reports `legacy-submit-failed`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n1. Replace native custom-event writers with the interrupt terminal.\n2. Render bound `interrupts` instead of `pendingInterrupts`.\n3. Replace boolean approval helpers with `resolveInterrupt` + explicit\n   denial/cancellation.\n4. Replace approval loops with atomic batch staging or root `resolveInterrupts`.\n5. Keep `addToolResult` for client-tool results where useful.\n6. Test expired items and failed transport before removing legacy support.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Migration\nid: interrupts-migration\norder: 6\ndescription: \"Migrate approval and resume code from legacy custom events and raw resume APIs to typed, atomic AG-UI interrupts.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai migration\n  - ag-ui interrupts\n  - addToolApprovalResponse\n  - pendingInterrupts\n  - resumeInterrupts\n---\n\nTanStack AI now models approvals, generic pauses, and client-tool execution as\nAG-UI interrupt descriptors. Native runs end with\n`RUN_FINISHED.outcome.type === 'interrupt'`, and the continuation is a new run\nwhose `parentRunId` is the interrupted run.\n\nThere is no codemod. Migrate the server lifecycle and client rendering together.\nLegacy readers stay temporarily for old streams but cannot provide the full\nnative contract. Start from [Overview](./overview).\n\n## API mapping\n\n| Deprecated / legacy | Current |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pendingInterrupts` | `interrupts` (`pendingInterrupts` is a deprecated alias of the same array) |\n| `ChatClient.getPendingInterrupts()` | `ChatClient.getInterrupts()` |\n| `addToolApprovalResponse({ id, approved })` | Find the bound `tool-approval` item, call `interrupt.resolveInterrupt(approved)` |\n| Raw `resumeInterrupts(entries, state)` | Bound item methods or root `resolveInterrupts(...)`; reserve `resumeInterruptsUnsafe` for validated recovery tooling |\n| `approval-requested` custom event | `RUN_FINISHED` interrupt descriptor, reason `tool_call` |\n| `tool-input-available` custom event | `RUN_FINISHED` interrupt descriptor, reason `tanstack:client_tool_execution` |\n| Boolean denial treated as cancellation | `resolveInterrupt(false)` for denial; `cancel()` for payloadless cancellation |\n\n`addToolResult` is **not** removed. It still handles client-tool results and\ndelegates to a matching native item. `needsApproval` remains the tool-definition\nswitch for approvals.\n\n## Single approval\n\n```ts ignore\n// Before\nawait addToolApprovalResponse({ id: approval.id, approved: true })\n\n// After\nconst interrupt = interrupts.find(\n  (item) => item.kind === 'tool-approval' && item.toolName === 'transfer',\n)\nif (interrupt?.kind === 'tool-approval' && interrupt.toolName === 'transfer') {\n  interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true)\n}\n```\n\nA valid singleton submits automatically. For the full render/resolve component\nsee [Tool Approval](./tool-approval).\n\n## Branch payloads and edits\n\nLegacy boolean approvals couldn't carry typed data. Add `approvalSchema` and\nresolve the selected branch with data under `payload`:\n\n```ts ignore\ninterrupt.resolveInterrupt(true, {\n  editedArgs: { amount: 12, recipient: 'Ada' }, // optional, approval-only, full replacement\n  payload: { note: 'Reviewed' },\n})\ninterrupt.resolveInterrupt(false, { payload: { reason: 'Policy limit' } })\n```\n\nRejection never accepts edits; top-level custom fields are invalid. A single\n`approvalSchema` (not `{ approve, reject }`) applies to the selected decision;\nwith no schema the boolean shorthand stays valid.\n\n## Denial vs cancellation\n\n`resolveInterrupt(false, ...)` continues the model with an explicit rejected\ndecision. `cancel()` emits AG-UI `status: 'cancelled'` and never validates or\nselects the reject branch. Deprecated `addToolApprovalResponse({ approved: false })`\nmaps to denial, not cancellation.\n\n## Batches\n\nNative batches are all-or-nothing. Replace approval-ID loops with staged items\n(the last valid item auto-submits) or one synchronous root callback:\n\n```ts ignore\nresolveInterrupts((interrupt) => {\n  if (interrupt.kind === 'tool-approval') {\n    interrupt.resolveInterrupt(true, { payload: { note: 'Batch review' } })\n    return\n  }\n  interrupt.cancel()\n})\n```\n\n`resolveInterrupts(true|false)` is shorthand only for all-approval batches with\nno payload/edits. Use `cancelInterrupts()` for payloadless all-items cancel,\n`clearResolution()` to drop one draft, `retryInterrupts()` only when every item\nis still validly staged and the root error is retryable. See\n[Multiple Interrupts](./multiple).\n\n## Generic responses\n\nDon't derive a static type from a received `responseSchema`. Parse as\n`unknown`, convert with `z.fromJSONSchema`, then resolve the validated value.\nFull form example in [Generic Interrupts](./generic).\n\n## Server events\n\nA native server emits, in order: `MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT` → optional\n`STATE_SNAPSHOT` → `RUN_FINISHED` with a nonempty interrupt outcome.\nContinuations use a fresh `runId`, the same `threadId`, and the interrupted run\nas `parentRunId`, with every pending ID present exactly once.\n\nInterrupts run **ephemerally**: the server reconstructs and validates the\nexpected batch from the submitted history and its current tool definitions, so\na stateless route needs no persistence. Because the batch is rebuilt from\nclient-provided input, this mode does not provide authoritative recovery,\nexactly-once, replay protection, or restart recovery.\n\n`resumeInterruptsUnsafe` is a low-level escape hatch for submitting validated\nraw resume entries directly, not the normal target for approval UI.\n\n## Legacy limits\n\nDeprecated readers recognize well-formed historical `approval-requested` and\n`tool-input-available` events and convert a fully-covered legacy batch into one\ncloned-history follow-up. They do **not** support edited arguments, custom\napproval payloads, generic responses, payloadless cancellation, or expiry/\nschema-hash reconciliation; those fail with `legacy-unsupported`. Native and\nlegacy items cannot mix in one batch; a failed legacy transport keeps staged\ndecisions and reports `legacy-submit-failed`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n1. Replace native custom-event writers with the interrupt terminal.\n2. Render bound `interrupts` instead of `pendingInterrupts`.\n3. Replace boolean approval helpers with `resolveInterrupt` + explicit\n   denial/cancellation.\n4. Replace approval loops with atomic batch staging or root `resolveInterrupts`.\n5. Keep `addToolResult` for client-tool results where useful.\n6. Test expired items and failed transport before removing legacy support.\n"}
